.TH "PB-PREVIEW-REPLAY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview-replay - Deliberately replay one retained HTTP request to the same origin


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview replay <preview> <capture-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Deliberately replay one retained HTTP request to the same origin

.PP
Replay one retained HTTP request to the same preview origin by capture ID. This deliberately repeats an HTTP action; use an idempotency key when the origin supports one.

.PP
A preview exposes a local target through a temporary Paperboat URL or private/team access policy. Inspect its status before sharing the URL, and stop or delete it when no longer needed. Browser HTTP terminates TLS at the edge.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for replay

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	explicit idempotency key for safe retry (generated when omitted)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-preview(1)\fP
